{"results":[{"url":"https://www.facebook.com/27news/posts/although-franchise-owners-have-to-abide-by-certain-guidelines-in-their-agreement/963599969133093/","final_url":"https://www.facebook.com/27news/posts/although-franchise-owners-have-to-abide-by-certain-guidelines-in-their-agreement/963599969133093/","title":"WKOW 27","description":"Although franchise owners have to abide by certain guidelines in their agreements with the parent company, they are free to invite political candidates to serve fries without McDonald’s buy-in.","language":"en","text":"Although franchise owners have to abide by certain guidelines in their agreements with the parent company, they are free to invite political candidates to serve fries without McDonald’s buy-in.\n\nAll reactions:\n\n81 comments\n\n1 share\n\nLike\n\nComment\n\nMost relevant\n\n\n\nKent Ritchie\n\nAnd the next day a large e-coli outbreak linked to McDonald's is reported. If that's not an omen, I don't know what is.\n\nView 1 reply\n\nLinda Ladwig\n\nI was wondering about that. It's the difference between a corporate-owned restaurant and a franchisee-owned one.\n\n1\n\nWilliam Cashman\n\nWHERE HE BELONGS.\n\n3\n\nView all 5 replies\n\nThomas Joyce\n\nHow is this news?\n\nWe all know the restaurant was closed. The whole thing just another ridiculous republican hoax.\n\n6\n\nView 1 reply","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":5569.9899189930875,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}